  "question": {
    "text": "In a face centred cubic lattice, atom A occupies the corner positions and atom B occupies the face centre positions. If one atom of $B$ is missing from one of the face centred points, the formula of the compound is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9vFta",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{AB}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Jy4ci",
      "text": "\n$A_2 B_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yGpkU",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{A}_2 \\mathrm{~B}_5$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4j89B",
      "text": "\n$A_2 B$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Effective no.of $A$ atoms $=\\frac{1}{8} \\times 8=1$\nEffective no.of $B$ atoms $=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 5$ (One is missing) $=\\frac{5}{2}$\nTherefore formula is $A_1 B_{\\frac{5}{2}}=A_2 B_5$",
    "image": null
  },
